/* Manu Tere · zh · pack cook · generated by build.py; loaded with the pack */
__mtLangPack('zh','cook',{"The track starts at the end of the Avatiu valley road, in the north. Soon the path splits three ways.":"步道从北部 Avatiu 山谷公路的尽头开始。没走多久，小路就分成了三条。","Follow the orange triangles nailed to the trees.":"跟着钉在树上的橙色三角标志走。","The stream crosses the track again and again.":"溪流一次又一次地横穿步道。","Cross on the stones":"踩着石头过河",": tap the flat, dry ones, in order. Mossy green stones are slippery.":"：按顺序点击平坦、干燥的石头。长着绿苔的石头很滑。","Another fork in the forest. Hikers get lost here every year.":"森林里又出现一个岔路口。每年都有徒步者在这里迷路。","Find the orange triangle.":"找到橙色三角标志。","Now the steep part: the path climbs a ridge of roots and wet rock.":"现在是陡峭的一段：小路沿着一道布满树根和湿岩石的山脊向上爬。","Tap each root":"点击每一条树根","to pull yourself up, the glowing one first.":"，把自己拉上去，先点发光的那条。","You are on the ridge, at the foot of":"你来到山脊上，就在",", the Needle, a spire of rock about {#1} m high. The view runs over the whole island to the reef. Your guide asks: shall we climb the Needle itself?":"，也就是“针峰”的脚下。这是一座约 {#1} m 高的石尖。从这里可以望见整座岛，一直望到礁石。你的向导问：我们要爬上针峰顶吗？","Down the southern side, the forest is wetter.":"往南侧下山，森林更加潮湿。","Keep to the orange triangles.":"沿着橙色三角标志走。","The track ends at":"步道的终点是",", Papua, in the south. You are hot and muddy. Your guide reminds you that the streams of the valley flow into the island’s drinking water.":"，位于南部的 Papua。你又热又满身是泥。向导提醒你：山谷里的溪流会流进岛上的饮用水。","The Cross-Island Track in the forest of Rarotonga":"Rarotonga 森林中的穿岛步道","The orange triangle: this way.":"橙色三角标志：走这边。","No triangle on that tree: that path fades into the bush. Look again.":"那棵树上没有三角标志：那条小路会消失在灌木丛里。再看看。","That stone is covered in moss: your foot would slip. Choose a grey, dry one.":"那块石头长满了苔藓：你的脚会打滑。选一块灰色、干燥的。","One stone at a time: take the next one, the glowing one.":"一次踩一块石头：踩下一块，发光的那块。","Not that one: hold the next root, the glowing one, so you always have three points on the rock.":"不是那条：抓住下一条树根，发光的那条，这样你始终有三个点贴着岩石。","The ridge!":"到山脊了！","Yes, climb to the top of the Needle":"要，爬上针峰顶","No: rest at its foot, look, and go on":"不要：在它脚下休息、看看风景，然后继续走","Yes. The spire itself needs real rock climbing, with ropes. Walkers stop at its foot, where the view is already wide.":"对。针峰本身需要真正的攀岩，要用绳索。徒步者在它脚下止步，那里的视野已经很开阔了。","The Needle is a sheer spire: reaching its top is rock climbing, with ropes and training. Walkers stay at its foot.":"针峰是一座陡峭的石尖：登顶属于攀岩，需要绳索和训练。徒步者只在它脚下停留。","Wash with soap under the falls":"在瀑布下用肥皂洗澡","Rinse off in the pool, without soap or sunscreen":"在水潭里冲一冲，不用肥皂，也不涂防晒霜","Yes: the streams of the valley feed the island’s drinking water. A swim, nothing more.":"对：山谷里的溪流是岛上饮用水的水源。游个泳就好，别的什么都不做。","This water goes on to the island’s taps: no soap, no shampoo, no sunscreen.":"这些水会流到岛上的水龙头里：不用肥皂，不用洗发水，不涂防晒霜。","You crossed Rarotonga on foot, from the Avatiu valley in the north to Wigmore’s waterfall in the south, past Te Rua Manga, the Needle. The track takes about half a day: follow the orange triangles, cross the streams on dry stones, and go with a guide or a friend, never alone in the rain.":"你徒步穿越了 Rarotonga，从北部的 Avatiu 山谷走到南部的 Wigmore 瀑布，途经 Te Rua Manga，也就是针峰。这条步道大约要走半天：跟着橙色三角标志走，踩着干燥的石头过溪，和向导或朋友同行，下雨时千万不要独自前往。","A forest valley of the Takitumu Conservation Area, Rarotonga":"Rarotonga Takitumu 保护区的一处森林山谷","You join the volunteers in the <b>Takitumu Conservation Area</b>, in the south of Rarotonga. Before the birds nest, from October, the rats must be kept down: they eat the eggs and the chicks in the nests. <b>Refill each bait station</b> along the trail: a closed tube, so only rats reach the bait.":"你加入了 Rarotonga 南部 <b>Takitumu 保护区</b>的志愿者。从十月起，鸟儿筑巢之前，必须控制老鼠的数量：它们会吃掉巢里的蛋和雏鸟。<b>给沿路的每个投饵站补充鼠饵</b>：投饵站是封闭的管子，只有老鼠才能吃到鼠饵。","<b>The census.</b> Every three years the birds are counted. Many wear coloured rings on their legs, so each bird can be told apart. For each kākerōri that lands, decide: <b>a new bird</b>, young (still orange, under four) or adult (grey), or <b>already counted</b> (the same rings as one in your notebook).":"<b>数鸟调查。</b>每三年统计一次鸟的数量。许多鸟腿上戴着彩色脚环，这样就能分辨每一只鸟。每有一只 kākerōri 落下，就做出判断：是<b>新的鸟</b>，幼鸟（还是橙色，不到四岁）还是成鸟（灰色），或者<b>已经数过</b>（脚环和你笔记本上的某一只相同）。","Notebook: empty.":"笔记本：空白。","Bird {A} of {B}. Look at its colour and its rings, then check your notebook.":"第 {A} 只鸟，共 {B} 只。看看它的颜色和脚环，再查一查你的笔记本。","New · young":"新 · 幼鸟","New · adult":"新 · 成鸟","Yes: the same rings are in your notebook. Counted once.":"对：你的笔记本里有同样的脚环。只数一次。","Yes: still orange, a young bird.":"对：还是橙色的，是一只幼鸟。","Yes: grey, at least four years old.":"对：灰色的，至少四岁了。","Look at the notebook: these rings are already there. A bird is counted only once.":"看看笔记本：这些脚环已经记下了。每只鸟只数一次。","These rings are not in your notebook yet: a new bird.":"这些脚环还没记在你的笔记本里：是一只新的鸟。","Some orange still: a young bird, under four.":"还带着一些橙色：是一只幼鸟，不到四岁。","All grey: an adult.":"全身灰色：是一只成鸟。","Your count: <b>{A} kākerōri</b>, {B} young and {C} adults, with {D} of {E} right calls. Young birds mean the nests are working: the rats were kept away.":"你的统计：<b>{A} 只 kākerōri</b>，其中幼鸟 {B} 只、成鸟 {C} 只，{E} 次判断中答对了 {D} 次。有幼鸟说明鸟巢很安全：老鼠被挡在了外面。","You helped the volunteers of Takitumu: bait stations refilled before the nesting season, then a count with the rings on the birds’ legs. In {#1} fewer than {#2} kākerōri were left; about {#3} were counted on Rarotonga in {#4}, and a second group lives on Atiu. The kākerōri is now in your bird book.":"你帮助了 Takitumu 的志愿者：在筑巢季节之前补充了投饵站，然后借助鸟腿上的脚环做了一次统计。{#1} 年时只剩下不到 {#2} 只 kākerōri；{#4} 年在 Rarotonga 统计到约 {#3} 只，另外还有一群生活在 Atiu。kākerōri 现在已收入你的鸟类图鉴。","Drummers under the trees of an open-air stage, Rarotonga":"Rarotonga 一座露天舞台的树下，鼓手们正在演奏","<b>Round {A} of {B}.</b> Listen: the <b>pate taki</b>, the lead drummer, plays the call.":"<b>第 {A} 轮，共 {B} 轮。</b>仔细听：领头鼓手 <b>pate taki</b> 敲出呼唤。","Pate · wood":"Pate · 木","Paʻu · skin":"Paʻu · 皮","Not quite: listen again.":"不太对：再听一遍。","The dancers move to your answer!":"舞者们随着你的回应起舞！","The <b>ʻura paʻu</b>, the drum dance, begins. The women tell the story with their hips and their hands, the sea, the birds, the flowers; the men flap their knees in a half crouch, upper bodies still.":"鼓舞 <b>ʻura paʻu</b> 开始了。女人们用臀部和双手讲述故事：大海、鸟儿、花朵；男人们半蹲着拍打双膝，上身保持不动。","You answered the pate taki, the lead drummer, on the pate and the paʻu, and the dancers danced the ʻura paʻu{A}. A drum group has a lead drummer, a second, players on the wooden gongs (tokere) and on the skin drums (paʻu). The ʻura, with its legends and its action songs, the kaparima, is danced at every festival.":"你用 pate 和 paʻu 回应了领头鼓手 pate taki，舞者们跳起了 ʻura paʻu{A}。一个鼓乐队有一位领头鼓手、一位副鼓手，还有敲木锣（tokere）和皮鼓（paʻu）的鼓手。ʻura 连同它的传说和动作歌曲 kaparima，在每个节庆上都会表演。","Evening in Rarotonga. Under the trees, a drum group warms up for the dancers. You sit with the drummers: two drums are yours, the <b>pate</b>, a slit drum of wood with a sharp, high voice, and the <b>paʻu</b>, a skin drum, low and round.":"Rarotonga 的傍晚。树下，一个鼓乐队正在为舞者热身。你和鼓手们坐在一起：有两面鼓归你，<b>pate</b> 是木制裂缝鼓，声音清脆高亢；<b>paʻu</b> 是皮鼓，声音低沉圆润。","A tīvaevae being made on a floor mat":"在地席上制作中的一床 tīvaevae","Row {A} of 7. The taʻunga calls the colours: <b>{B}</b>. Thread your squares on the cotton in that order.":"第 {A} 行，共 7 行。taʻunga 报出颜色：<b>{B}</b>。按这个顺序把你的方块穿到棉线上。","Listen to the taʻunga: next comes":"听 taʻunga 的：下一个是","A strand ready.":"一串穿好了。","The vaʻine tini, the sewing group, lay each strand on the floor to see how it fits. <b>Tap the mat</b> to lay your row.":"缝纫小组 vaʻine tini 把每一串摆在地上，看看是否合适。<b>点击地席</b>，铺上你的这一行。","The tiare māori is in bloom on the mat. For the border, the manu has an idea: <b>“Put me on it, flying!”</b> What does the taʻunga say?":"tiare māori 在地席上盛开了。manu 想到一个主意，要用在边框上：<b>“把我缝上去，正在飞的样子！”</b>taʻunga 会怎么说？","“Yes, a bird brings good luck.”":"“好啊，鸟会带来好运。”","“No bird on a bedspread: leaves and flowers instead.”":"“床罩上不放鸟：换成叶子和花吧。”","Yes. Animal and bird shapes are thought unlucky on a bedspread: tīvaevae bloom with the flowers and leaves of the islands.":"对。人们认为床罩上的动物和鸟的图案不吉利：tīvaevae 上盛开的是岛上的花和叶子。","Not on a bedspread: there, bird and animal shapes are thought unlucky.":"床罩上不行：人们认为那上面的鸟和动物图案不吉利。","The block is done: the women will sew it with many others onto the backing cloth. It may take months.":"这一块完成了：妇女们会把它和许多其他块一起缝到衬布上。这可能要花好几个月。",", without one wrong square":"，一块方块也没有放错","You threaded a block of a tīvaevae taʻōrei, a patchwork quilt, in the order the taʻunga called{A}. Tīvaevae are made together by groups of women and given at the great moments of life: weddings, a boy’s haircutting ceremony, the welcome of a minister, a funeral.":"你按照 taʻunga 报出的顺序，穿好了一块 tīvaevae taʻōrei（拼布被）{A}。Tīvaevae 由妇女们一起制作，在人生的重要时刻赠送：婚礼、男孩的剪发仪式、迎接牧师、葬礼。","In a village hall of Rarotonga, the vaʻine tini, the women’s sewing group, are making a <b>tīvaevae taʻōrei</b>, a quilt of hundreds of little squares. The taʻunga, the master of the pattern, has drawn a <b>tiare māori</b>. She calls the colours; each woman threads her squares.":"在 Rarotonga 的一座村礼堂里，缝纫小组 vaʻine tini 正在制作一床 <b>tīvaevae taʻōrei</b>，这是一床由数百个小方块拼成的被子。图案大师 taʻunga 画了一朵 <b>tiare māori</b>。她报出颜色，每位妇女穿起自己的方块。","Take a needle":"拿起一根针","The giant clam nursery of Aitutaki":"Aitutaki 的砗磲苗圃","At the Aitutaki Marine Research Centre, young paʻua grow in sunny tanks. Today some go out to the lagoon. <b>Choose the five healthy ones</b>: a bright blue mantle, open to the sun, sitting firm on their base. A pale clam has lost the tiny algae that feed it; a tipped one is not holding on.":"在 Aitutaki 海洋研究中心，幼小的 paʻua 在阳光充足的水槽里生长。今天有一些要放归泻湖。<b>选出五只健康的</b>：外套膜呈鲜亮的蓝色，向着阳光张开，稳稳地立在底座上。颜色苍白的砗磲失去了喂养它的微小藻类；翻倒的那只则还没有抓牢。","Too pale: this one has lost the algae that live in its mantle and feed it. It stays in the tank to recover.":"太苍白了：它失去了生活在外套膜里、为它提供养分的藻类。它要留在水槽里恢复。","Tipped over and loose: it is not holding on yet. Leave it a few more weeks.":"翻倒了，松松垮垮：它还没有抓牢。再给它几个星期吧。","A healthy one.":"一只健康的。","Out by boat to the lagoon ridge. <b>Set each clam in a good place</b>: wedged in the coral, so the waves cannot roll it, and in full sun, because the algae in its mantle need light.":"乘船出发，前往泻湖中的礁脊。<b>把每只砗磲放在合适的地方</b>：牢牢卡在珊瑚里，这样海浪就推不动它；还要晒得到充足的阳光，因为它外套膜里的藻类需要光。","Loose sand: the next swell would roll the clam away. Find coral.":"松软的沙子：下一阵涌浪就会把砗磲卷走。找找珊瑚。","In the shade of the ledge the clam would starve: it lives on the sunlight caught by its algae.":"在岩檐的阴影里，砗磲会饿死：它靠藻类捕获的阳光生活。","Wedged firm, in the sun.":"牢牢卡住，晒得到太阳。","A visitor asks when the clams you set today may be taken. What does the centre say?":"一位游客问，你今天放下的砗磲什么时候可以采收。中心会怎么回答？","Not for years: a paʻua only begins to breed at {#1} to {#2} years old, and the island’s rules decide":"很多年内都不行：paʻua 要到 {#1} 至 {#2} 岁才开始繁殖，而且由岛上的规定来决定","Yes. A clam must breed many times first. Overharvesting once emptied the lagoons: today export limits, island by-laws and raʻui protect them.":"对。砗磲必须先繁殖很多次。过度采捕曾让泻湖空空如也：如今出口限额、岛上的法规和 raʻui 都在保护它们。","Next season, once they are as big as a hand":"下个季节，等它们长到手掌那么大的时候","Far too soon: a paʻua only begins to breed at {#1} to {#2} years old.":"太早了：paʻua 要到 {#1} 至 {#2} 岁才开始繁殖。","Any time, the lagoon is full of them":"随时都可以，泻湖里多的是","They were once overharvested in the Cook Islands: that is why the hatchery exists.":"它们在库克群岛曾经被过度采捕：这正是建立孵化场的原因。","You chose five healthy young paʻua in the tanks and set them in the coral of the lagoon ridge, in full sun. The hatchery of the Aitutaki Marine Research Centre has raised giant clams since {#1}; in {#2} about {#3} young clams went out to the lagoon in one month.":"你在水槽里选出了五只健康的 paʻua 幼贝，把它们放进泻湖礁脊的珊瑚里，晒得到充足的阳光。Aitutaki 海洋研究中心的孵化场自 {#1} 年起培育砗磲；{#2} 年，一个月内就有约 {#3} 只幼贝被放归泻湖。","A paʻua, a giant clam":"一只 paʻua，即砗磲","Its mantle is blue and green: tiny algae live in it and feed it with sunlight.":"它的外套膜是蓝绿色的：微小的藻类生活在里面，用阳光喂养它。","An ʻonu, a green turtle":"一只 ʻonu，即绿海龟","Turtles graze the seagrass and rest in the lagoon. Keep a few metres away and let it swim past.":"海龟在泻湖里啃食海草、休息。保持几米的距离，让它游过去。","A parrotfish":"一条鹦嘴鱼","It scrapes algae off dead coral with its beak; the white sand of the lagoon is partly ground coral that it has eaten.":"它用喙从死珊瑚上刮下藻类；泻湖的白沙有一部分就是它吃下又磨碎的珊瑚。","A school of trevally":"一群鲹鱼","Fast silver hunters of the lagoon. In a raʻui they grow big, and their young spread out to the reefs nearby.":"泻湖里身手敏捷的银色猎手。在 raʻui 里它们能长得很大，幼鱼还会扩散到附近的礁石。","A sea cucumber":"一只海参","It sifts the sand for food and leaves it cleaner. Sea cucumbers too are protected by raʻui on some islands.":"它筛滤沙子寻找食物，让沙子变得更干净。在一些岛上，海参也受到 raʻui 的保护。","Branching coral":"枝状珊瑚","Alive, growing a few centimetres a year. Never stand on it: float above, fins up.":"它是活的，每年长几厘米。千万不要站在上面：浮在它上方，脚蹼朝上。","A big cowrie shell lies on the sand, perfect for a necklace.":"一个大大的宝螺壳躺在沙子上，做项链再合适不过了。","Yes: in a raʻui nothing is taken, not even a shell. Look, take a photo.":"对：在 raʻui 里什么都不能拿，连一个贝壳也不行。看一看，拍张照吧。","Take just this one":"只拿这一个","In a raʻui nothing at all is taken, not even one shell.":"在 raʻui 里什么都不能拿，连一个贝壳也不行。","You are tired. There is a flat coral head just below you.":"你累了。你正下方有一块平平的珊瑚丘。","Float on your back to rest":"仰浮在水面上休息","Yes. Coral is alive: standing on it breaks it, and it can cut you too.":"对。珊瑚是活的：站在上面会把它踩断，它也可能割伤你。","Stand on the coral to rest":"站在珊瑚上休息","Coral is alive and breaks under your feet. Float to rest.":"珊瑚是活的，会在你脚下断裂。浮在水面上休息吧。","The turtle swims close by.":"海龟从你身边游过。","Yes: a few metres away, no touching, no chasing.":"对：保持几米距离，不触摸，不追赶。","Hold its shell for a ride":"抓住它的壳搭个便车","Never touch or chase a turtle: it needs to come up to breathe without fear.":"千万不要触摸或追赶海龟：它需要毫无畏惧地浮上来呼吸。","Under the water of a raʻui, the lagoon of Aitutaki":"在 raʻui 的水下，Aitutaki 的泻湖","This part of the lagoon is a <b>raʻui</b>: the chiefs have closed it, so that the clams, the fish and the shells can grow back. You may swim and look; you may take <b>nothing</b>. <b>Tap each creature</b> to take its photo.":"这片泻湖是一个 <b>raʻui</b>：首领们把它封闭起来，让砗磲、鱼和贝壳重新长起来。你可以游泳、观看，但<b>什么都不能拿</b>。<b>点击每一种生物</b>，给它拍张照片。","You swam in a raʻui of the Aitutaki lagoon and took only photos: a paʻua, a turtle, a parrotfish, trevally, a sea cucumber and living coral. A raʻui is an old way of caring for the sea: the chiefs close a reef or a lagoon for a time, and when it opens again, it is full.":"你在 Aitutaki 泻湖的 raʻui 里游泳，只拍了照片：一只 paʻua、一只海龟、一条鹦嘴鱼、鲹鱼、一只海参和活的珊瑚。raʻui 是一种古老的护海方式：首领们把一片礁石或泻湖封闭一段时间，等它重新开放时，里面又满满当当了。","a turquoise channel over white sand":"白沙上的一条碧绿水道","brown and dark: coral heads just under the surface":"褐色而暗沉：水面下就是珊瑚丘","pale, almost white: a sandbank, too shallow":"浅淡、几乎发白：是沙洲，太浅了","The lagoon of Aitutaki seen from a small boat":"从小船上看 Aitutaki 的泻湖","You take a small boat across the lagoon of Aitutaki, towards":"你乘小船穿过 Aitutaki 的泻湖，驶向",", One Foot Island, in the south-east. The skipper hands you the tiller.":"，也就是东南方的一脚岛（One Foot Island）。船长把舵柄交给了你。","{A}<b>Read the colour of the water</b> and choose the way ahead ({B} of {C}).":"{A}<b>看清海水的颜色</b>，选择前进的方向（{B} / {C}）。","Deep water is safe, but the channel to the motu is the turquoise one over the sand.":"深水很安全，但通往 motu 的水道是白沙上那条碧绿色的。","Not that way: {A}.{B}":"不是那边：{A}。{B}","The turquoise channel: sand below, deep enough.":"碧绿色的水道：下面是沙子，水也够深。","You run the boat gently onto the sand of <b>Tapuaetai</b>, One Foot Island. Its name, it is said, comes from a single footprint left in the sand. A little hut on the motu stamps a foot in visitors’ passports: your passport has one now.":"你把船轻轻地开上了 <b>Tapuaetai</b>（一脚岛）的沙滩。据说它的名字来自沙滩上留下的一个脚印。motu 上的一间小屋会在游客的护照上盖一个脚印：现在你的护照上也有一个了。",", without one wrong turn":"，一次也没走错","You crossed the lagoon of Aitutaki to Tapuaetai, One Foot Island, reading the water: turquoise over sand is the channel, brown means coral heads, white a sandbank, deep blue the open water{A}. The lagoon of Aitutaki covers more than 50 km², with fifteen motu on its rim.":"你看着海水的颜色，穿过 Aitutaki 的泻湖来到 Tapuaetai（一脚岛）：白沙上的碧绿色是水道，褐色是珊瑚丘，白色是沙洲，深蓝色是开阔水域{A}。Aitutaki 的泻湖面积超过 50 km²，边缘环绕着十五个 motu。","Inside Anatakitaki cave, Atiu, by headlamp":"在 Atiu 的 Anatakitaki 洞穴里，借着头灯的光","After a walk through the forest of the makatea, your guide leads you into <b>Anatakitaki</b>. It is pitch dark. <b>Keep your lamp on the ground</b> and step from stone to stone, the glowing one next. Up on the ceiling the kōpeka have their nests: never shine your lamp at them.":"穿过 makatea 的森林之后，向导带你走进 <b>Anatakitaki</b>。洞里漆黑一片。<b>让灯光照着地面</b>，从一块石头踩到另一块，下一块是发光的那块。洞顶上是 kōpeka 的巢：千万不要用灯照它们。","Lamp down! The light on the ceiling disturbs the kōpeka on their nests.":"灯往下照！照到洞顶的光会打扰巢里的 kōpeka。","One stone at a time: the glowing one.":"一次踩一块石头：踩发光的那块。","Deep in the cave the guide says: <b>lamps off</b>. Listen. The kōpeka fly in the dark and find their way by <b>clicks</b>, echoes off the rock. <b>Tap the button each time you hear one.</b>":"在洞穴深处，向导说：<b>关灯</b>。仔细听。kōpeka 在黑暗中飞行，靠<b>咔嗒声</b>在岩石上的回声找路。<b>每听到一声，就点击一次按钮。</b>","Turn off my lamp":"关掉我的灯","I hear a click!":"我听到一声咔嗒！","You heard <b>{A}</b> of {B} clicks. The kōpeka do not use their clicks to find food, only to find their way in the dark, back to a nest on the rock where no light ever reaches.":"{B} 声咔嗒中，你听到了 <b>{A}</b> 声。kōpeka 不用咔嗒声寻找食物，只用它在黑暗中找路，回到岩石上那个从来照不到光的巢。","At the end, an underground pool of clear water, lit by candles. Your guide asks: what will you do with the kōpeka nests above the pool?":"尽头是一个清澈的地下水潭，点着蜡烛。向导问你：水潭上方的 kōpeka 巢，你打算怎么办？","Take one empty nest home, as a souvenir":"拿一个空巢回家，当作纪念品","Leave them all, swim quietly, and go":"一个都不动，安静地游一会儿，然后离开","Yes. There are fewer than {#1} kōpeka in the world, all on Atiu.":"对。全世界的 kōpeka 不到 {#1} 只，全都在 Atiu。",", without once shining on a nest":"，一次也没有照到鸟巢","You went into Anatakitaki with a guide of Atiu, lamp on the ground, and listened to the kōpeka in the dark{A}. The kōpeka, the Atiu swiftlet, lives nowhere else: fewer than 400 birds, in two caves of the makatea. They leave at dawn to hunt insects over the lake and the gardens, and come home from about half past six in the evening.":"你跟着一位 Atiu 的向导走进 Anatakitaki，灯光照着地面，在黑暗中聆听 kōpeka{A}。kōpeka，即阿蒂乌金丝燕，别处都没有：不到 400 只，栖息在 makatea 的两个洞穴里。它们黎明时出洞，在湖面和菜园上空捕食昆虫，傍晚大约六点半起陆续回家。","Never: a nest may be used again, and the kōpeka are protected. Take only the memory.":"千万不要：鸟巢可能会被再次使用，而且 kōpeka 受到保护。只把回忆带走吧。","Dawn on Atiu: wooden boxes with lorikeets ready to be released":"Atiu 的黎明：装着吸蜜鹦鹉的木箱准备放飞","Box {A} of {B}. <b>Hold the button</b> to lift the lid slowly. Let go too soon and you jerk the lid: the bird inside panics.":"第 {A} 个箱子，共 {B} 个。<b>按住按钮</b>，慢慢掀起箱盖。松手太早，箱盖就会猛地一动：里面的鸟会受到惊吓。","Hold to lift the lid":"按住掀起箱盖","Too sudden! Start again, slowly: the bird must come out when it is ready.":"太突然了！重新来，慢慢地：要等鸟准备好了再出来。","Out it climbs, looks around, and flies to the trees.":"它爬出来，四处张望，然后飞向树林。","Why were the kura brought to Atiu, and not to another island?":"为什么把 kura 带到 Atiu，而不是别的岛？","Atiu has no black rats, which raid the nests":"Atiu 没有会袭击鸟巢的黑家鼠","Yes. On Rimatara the last kura survived because of a tapu of its queen, around {#1}, and because the black rat never landed. Atiu has no black rats either.":"对。在 Rimatara，最后的 kura 之所以能存活下来，是因为大约 {#1} 年女王立下的一道 tapu，也因为黑家鼠从未登上那座岛。Atiu 也没有黑家鼠。","Atiu has the most coconut palms":"Atiu 的椰子树最多","Not the reason: the black rat is. Atiu was chosen because it has none.":"不是这个原因：原因是黑家鼠。选择 Atiu 是因为那里没有黑家鼠。","Atiu is the closest island to Rimatara":"Atiu 是离 Rimatara 最近的岛","Mangaia is closer to Rimatara. Atiu was chosen because it has no black rats.":"Mangaia 离 Rimatara 更近。选择 Atiu 是因为那里没有黑家鼠。","You met their cousins on Rimatara, where they are called ʻura.":"你在 Rimatara 见过它们的表亲，在那里它们叫作 ʻura。","You opened the boxes slowly at dawn, as the team did on 24 April 2007, when 27 kura from Rimatara were set free on Atiu. Hunted for their red feathers, the kura had vanished from the Cook Islands by the 1920s. The first chick was seen on Atiu in February 2008; by 2019 there were more than 400.{A}":"你在黎明时慢慢打开了箱子，就像 2007 年 4 月 24 日那支团队所做的那样：那一天，27 只来自 Rimatara 的 kura 在 Atiu 获得了自由。kura 因红色羽毛而遭到捕猎，到 1920 年代已从库克群岛消失。2008 年 2 月，Atiu 上出现了第一只雏鸟；到 2019 年，数量已超过 400 只。{A}","Dawn, {#1} April {#2}. A team has brought <b>{#3} kura</b>, the red lorikeet, from Rimatara, in the Australs, to Atiu. Once the kura lived here too, but people hunted them for their red feathers until none were left. Today they come home. <b>Open the boxes</b>, one by one, gently.":"{#2} 年 4 月 {#1} 日，黎明。一支团队把 <b>{#3} 只 kura</b>（红色的吸蜜鹦鹉）从南方群岛的 Rimatara 带到了 Atiu。kura 曾经也生活在这里，但人们为了它们的红色羽毛不断捕猎，直到一只也不剩。今天，它们回家了。<b>打开箱子</b>，一个接一个，轻轻地。","Go to the boxes":"走到箱子那里","Coffee bushes under the trees of Atiu":"Atiu 树下的咖啡树","In a coffee garden of Atiu, under the shade of bigger trees. Coffee is picked by hand: <b>only the ripe cherries, deep red</b>. Green and yellow ones stay on the branch to ripen.":"在 Atiu 的一座咖啡园里，在大树的树荫下。咖啡是手工采摘的：<b>只摘成熟的深红色咖啡果</b>。绿色和黄色的留在枝头继续成熟。","Still green: give it a few more weeks.":"还是绿的：再等几个星期吧。","Yellow, not yet red: almost ripe. Leave it.":"黄色，还没变红：快熟了。留着它。","Squeeze each cherry: the red skin slips off and two pale green beans come out, coated in a sweet slime. The beans rest a night in water to ferment and come clean. <b>Tap to squeeze</b>.":"挤压每一颗咖啡果：红色的果皮滑落，露出两颗浅绿色的咖啡豆，表面裹着一层甜甜的黏液。咖啡豆在水里泡一夜，发酵后就变干净了。<b>点击挤压</b>。","Squeeze a cherry":"挤一颗咖啡果","The beans dry in the sun for many days on a rack, raked often. <b>If a shower comes, cover them</b>, then open again when the sun is back.":"咖啡豆要放在架子上晒很多天太阳，还要经常翻耙。<b>如果下阵雨，就把它们盖起来</b>，等太阳出来再打开。","Cover the rack":"盖上架子","Open the rack":"打开架子","Rain on the beans! Cover them.":"雨落在咖啡豆上了！快盖起来。","The sun is back: open the rack.":"太阳出来了：打开架子。","The old way of Atiu: the beans are roasted in a pan <b>over an open fire, with a little coconut cream</b>, stirred all the time. Watch the colour: take them off the fire when they are <b>dark brown</b>, before they turn black.":"Atiu 的传统做法：咖啡豆放在锅里，<b>在明火上加一点椰浆</b>烘焙，要不停地翻炒。注意颜色：在豆子变黑之前、呈<b>深褐色</b>时，就把锅从火上拿开。","Take the pan off the fire":"把锅从火上拿开","Burnt! Start a new pan.":"烧焦了！重新烘一锅。","Still pale: these beans would taste green. Put them back on the fire.":"颜色还浅：这些豆子会有生涩味。放回火上。","Almost black: bitter. Start a new pan and take it off a little sooner.":"快变黑了：会发苦。重新烘一锅，早一点拿开。","Dark brown and fragrant.":"深褐色，香气扑鼻。","You picked only the red cherries, pulped them, dried the beans in the sun (covered from the showers) and roasted them dark brown over the fire, with coconut cream, the old way of Atiu. Coffee came to the Cook Islands with the missionaries in the {#1}th century. On Atiu it is grown without chemicals, picked and processed by hand, and roasted on the island.":"你只采摘了红色的咖啡果，去掉果肉，在阳光下晒干咖啡豆（下阵雨时盖好），再用 Atiu 的传统方法，加椰浆在火上烘成深褐色。咖啡在 {#1} 世纪随传教士来到库克群岛。在 Atiu，咖啡不用化学药品种植，手工采摘和加工，并在岛上烘焙。","The forest floor of Mangaia after rain":"雨后 Mangaia 的林地","It has rained all night on Mangaia: the best time to look for <b>pupu</b>, the little snail shells for an ʻei. <b>Lift the leaves and the stones</b> to find {A} shells, yellow and reddish-brown.":"Mangaia 下了一整夜的雨：这是寻找 <b>pupu</b> 的最好时机，pupu 是用来做 ʻei 的小蜗牛壳。<b>掀开树叶和石头</b>，找到 {A} 个黄色和红褐色的贝壳。","A pupu!":"一个 pupu！","Nothing under this one.":"这下面什么都没有。","Before they can be strung, the shells must be cleaned. How?":"贝壳在穿起来之前必须清理干净。怎么清理？","Scrub them hard with sand":"用沙子使劲擦洗","Boil them, or soak them for several days":"把它们煮一煮，或者浸泡好几天","Yes: boiled, or soaked for days, until they are clean.":"对：煮过，或者浸泡几天，直到干净为止。","They are tiny and thin: sand would crack them. They are boiled or soaked.":"它们又小又薄：沙子会把它们磨裂。要煮或者浸泡。","Now <b>pierce each shell</b> with a fine point, gently, one by one.":"现在用一根细针<b>给每个贝壳钻孔</b>，轻轻地，一个接一个。","String them in the pattern: <b>two yellow, one brown</b>, again and again (● yellow, ○ brown).":"按照图案穿起来：<b>两个黄色，一个褐色</b>，一遍又一遍（● 黄色，○ 褐色）。","Next comes {A} one.":"下一个是{A}的。","You gathered pupu after the rain, under leaves and stones, cleaned them, pierced them one by one and strung an ʻei pupu. A whole necklace takes hundreds of these little shells and many days: that is why an ʻei pupu is a precious gift.":"你在雨后从树叶和石头下面收集 pupu，把它们清理干净，一个一个钻孔，穿成了一串 ʻei pupu。一整条项链需要几百个这样的小贝壳，要花好多天：所以 ʻei pupu 是一份珍贵的礼物。","Taro terraces in a valley of Mangaia":"Mangaia 山谷里的芋头梯田","Mangaia was called <b>Aʻuaʻu ʻEnua</b>, “the island of terraces”. In its valleys, taro grows in the wet beds, fed by the streams. <b>Plant the taro tops</b> in the beds that stay wet: taro of the swamps needs its feet in water.":"Mangaia 曾被称为 <b>Aʻuaʻu ʻEnua</b>，意思是“梯田之岛”。在它的山谷里，芋头生长在湿润的田畦中，由溪水灌溉。<b>把芋头顶芽种</b>在保持湿润的田畦里：沼泽芋头的根要泡在水里。","Dry and cracked: this taro needs a wet bed.":"又干又裂：这株芋头需要湿润的田畦。","Months later the taro is ready. Cooked, peeled and pounded on a board with a stone pounder, it becomes <b>tiromi</b>, sold at the Friday morning market in Oneroa. <b>Tap to pound</b>, steadily.":"几个月后，芋头成熟了。煮熟、去皮，放在木板上用石杵捣烂，就变成了 <b>tiromi</b>，在 Oneroa 周五早上的市场上出售。<b>点击捣芋头</b>，节奏要稳。","You planted taro in the wet beds of a valley of Mangaia and pounded the cooked taro into tiromi. Mangaia’s old name, Aʻuaʻu ʻEnua, means “the island of terraces”: its taro swamps still feed the island, and tiromi is a treat of the Friday market.":"你在 Mangaia 山谷湿润的田畦里种下芋头，又把煮熟的芋头捣成了 tiromi。Mangaia 的旧名 Aʻuaʻu ʻEnua 意思是“梯田之岛”：它的芋头沼泽至今仍养活着全岛，而 tiromi 是周五市场上的美味。","The forest of the makatea, Mauke":"Mauke 的 makatea 森林","Mauke is called the garden island, and its makatea forest hides the <b>maire</b>, a thin vine with small shiny leaves and a sweet scent. <b>Find five maire vines</b>: look for the small paired leaves, and the scent.":"Mauke 被称为花园岛，它的 makatea 森林里藏着 <b>maire</b>，一种细细的藤蔓，叶子小而有光泽，散发着甜香。<b>找到五根 maire 藤</b>：留意成对的小叶子，还有香气。","Big leaves and no scent: not maire.":"叶子大，没有香味：不是 maire。","Back in the village, the bark of the vine is <b>peeled gently</b> with its leaves on, so that the green strands stay whole. <b>Tap along the vine</b>, from one end to the other.":"回到村里，带着叶子把藤的树皮<b>轻轻剥下</b>，好让绿色的藤条保持完整。<b>沿着藤蔓点击</b>，从一端到另一端。","Now <b>weave the strands together</b>, twist after twist, into a long garland. A full ʻei maire takes three or four hours.":"现在<b>把藤条编在一起</b>，一圈又一圈地拧，编成一条长长的花环。编一整条 ʻei maire 要三四个小时。","You found maire in the makatea forest of Mauke, peeled the strands and wove an ʻei maire, the garland of the garden island. Its sweet scent lasts about two weeks; ʻei maire are worn at the great moments: weddings, the opening of a church, the welcome of an honoured guest.":"你在 Mauke 的 makatea 森林里找到了 maire，剥下藤条，编成了一条 ʻei maire，花园岛的花环。它的甜香能保持大约两个星期；ʻei maire 在重要的时刻佩戴：婚礼、教堂落成、迎接尊贵的客人。","A small outrigger canoe off the reef of Mitiaro":"Mitiaro 礁石外的一艘小型舷外支架独木舟","The moon is right, and the old men say the <b>māroro</b>, the flying fish, are gathering off the reef. You paddle out in a small outrigger canoe, <b>no motor</b>, with a long-handled scoop net. <b>Scoop when the school passes under your net.</b>":"月相正合适，老人们说 <b>māroro</b>（飞鱼）正在礁石外聚集。你划着一艘小型舷外支架独木舟出海，<b>不用马达</b>，带着一张长柄抄网。<b>鱼群从网下游过时就抄网。</b>","Scoop!":"抄网！","A netful of māroro! ({A})":"满满一网 māroro！（{A}）","Too early or too late: wait for the school.":"太早或太晚了：等鱼群过来。","Back on shore with your catch. A visitor on the beach offers to <b>buy</b> the fish. What do you do?":"带着收获回到岸上。海滩上的一位游客想<b>买</b>这些鱼。你会怎么做？","Sell him a basket: it is a good price":"卖给他一篮：价钱不错","Say no: the māroro are shared with the island, never sold":"拒绝：māroro 要和全岛分享，从不出售","Yes. Every fish is shared among the people of Mitiaro: that is the rule of this fishery.":"对。每一条鱼都要分给 Mitiaro 的居民：这是这项渔业的规矩。","The māroro of Mitiaro may not be sold: the whole catch goes to the community.":"Mitiaro 的 māroro 不能出售：全部渔获都归社区所有。","<b>Share the catch</b>: one basket for each village.":"<b>分享渔获</b>：每个村子一篮。","You fished the māroro of Mitiaro the old way: a paddled outrigger canoe, a long-handled scoop net, a few days a month when the moon is right, from July to December. Nothing is sold: the whole catch is shared among the people of the island, and the fishery has lasted for generations.":"你用传统的方法捕捞 Mitiaro 的 māroro：划桨的舷外支架独木舟、长柄抄网，每个月在月相合适的几天出海，从七月到十二月。一条都不卖：全部渔获都分给岛上的居民，这项渔业已经延续了好几代人。","Pearl oyster lines in the lagoon of Manihiki":"Manihiki 泻湖里的珍珠贝养殖绳","On a pearl farm of Manihiki, the oysters hang on lines under the lagoon. Every few weeks a diver goes down to <b>clean them</b>: weed and little shells grow on them and slow them. <b>Hold to stay down</b> and clean; let go before your breath runs out.":"在 Manihiki 的一座珍珠养殖场，珍珠贝挂在泻湖水下的绳子上。每隔几个星期，潜水员就要下去<b>清理它们</b>：贝壳上会长出海藻和小贝壳，让它们长得更慢。<b>按住保持下潜</b>并清理；在憋不住气之前松手。","Hold: dive and clean":"按住：下潜并清理","Out of breath: come up! A diver always surfaces with air to spare.":"没气了：快上去！潜水员总是留着余气就浮上水面。","A blacktip shark glides by. The divers of the northern lagoons swim calmly among them.":"一条黑鳍礁鲨悠然游过。北部泻湖的潜水员们在它们中间从容地游动。","Back in the boat, a visitor asks why the farm keeps the lagoon so clean. What do you say?":"回到船上，一位游客问为什么养殖场要把泻湖保持得这么干净。你会怎么说？","The oysters filter the lagoon water: if it is dirty, they grow badly and the pearls too":"珍珠贝会过滤泻湖的水：水脏了，它们就长不好，珍珠也一样","Yes. A pearl lagoon lives on clean water; after Cyclone Martin in {#1} the farms had to start again almost from nothing.":"对。珍珠泻湖靠的是干净的水；{#1} 年 Martin 气旋过后，养殖场几乎是从零开始重建的。","So that tourists can see the bottom":"为了让游客看得见水底","Not the reason: the oysters live on the clean water they filter.":"不是这个原因：珍珠贝靠它们过滤的干净海水生活。","Clean water keeps the sharks away":"干净的水能把鲨鱼赶走","The blacktip sharks live in the lagoon anyway. The oysters need clean water to grow.":"黑鳍礁鲨反正都生活在泻湖里。珍珠贝需要干净的水才能生长。","You dived on the pearl lines of Manihiki, cleaning the oysters with your breath held, among the blacktip sharks of the lagoon. Manihiki lives from its black pearls: farms ring its deep lagoon, about {#1} km north of Rarotonga.":"你在 Manihiki 的珍珠养殖绳旁潜水，屏住呼吸清理珍珠贝，身边游着泻湖里的黑鳍礁鲨。Manihiki 靠黑珍珠为生：养殖场环绕着它深深的泻湖，这里位于 Rarotonga 以北约 {#1} km。","Young coconut palms on Tongareva":"Tongareva 的小椰子树","Rito comes from the <b>young frond still upright and unopened</b> at the heart of a coconut palm. Choose a <b>young palm</b>, so nobody has to climb, and cut its pale, closed frond.":"Rito 取自椰子树中心<b>还直立着、尚未展开的嫩叶</b>。选一棵<b>小椰子树</b>，这样就没人需要爬树，然后割下它那片浅色、闭合的嫩叶。","Too tall: you would have to climb. Rito is cut from young palms.":"太高了：你得爬上去。Rito 是从小椰子树上割的。","This frond has already opened and turned green: too late for rito.":"这片叶子已经展开、变绿了：做 rito 已经太迟了。","The fine fibres are separated from the leaves, cleaned and <b>boiled</b>. Then: a white hat, or a coloured one?":"把细纤维从叶子上分离出来，清理干净，再<b>煮一煮</b>。然后：做白帽子，还是彩色帽子？","White: bleach with lime juice":"白色：用青柠汁漂白","Coloured: dye the fibres":"彩色：给纤维染色","The weaving starts at the crown and works outwards, shaped on a <b>wooden hat mould</b>. The patterns are not written down: they are kept in the hands. <b>Weave each round</b>.":"编织从帽顶开始向外进行，在<b>木制帽模</b>上定型。图案不写在纸上：它们记在双手里。<b>一圈一圈地编</b>。","Weave a round":"编一圈","bleached them white with lime juice":"用青柠汁把它们漂白","dyed them":"把它们染了色","You cut rito from young palms on Tongareva, boiled the fibres, {A} and wove a rito hat from the crown outwards on a wooden mould. One hat takes about three days; the women weave together, singing and telling stories, and on Sunday the hats go to church.":"你在 Tongareva 从小椰子树上割下 rito，把纤维煮过，{A}，然后在木模上从帽顶向外编成了一顶 rito 帽。一顶帽子大约要三天；妇女们一起编织，边唱歌边讲故事，到了周日，帽子就戴着去教堂。"});
